    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The South Sudanese election commission has postponed the country's first presidential and parliamentary elections since independence in 2011.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-14:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The new date is February 11, 2027, moved from December 22, 2026, amid political tensions and continuing violence.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-14:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Elections have been postponed six times, to 2018, 2021, 2023, 2024, 2026, and finally the currently scheduled date in 2027. General elections are due to be held on 11 February 2027, the first since independence.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385800982:2",
        "wiki:rev:1385800982:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The report comes from AFP via RFI.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-14:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-14T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined it: “South Sudan postpones first-ever national elections until February.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:60bd50e5e1b7"
      ]
    },
    {
